{% extends "base.html.twig" %}

{% block title %}Card Game{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="container">
<h1>Card Game</h1>

<p>Welcome to the card game section. Here you can browse the deck, shuffle it and draw cards.</p>

<p>
    <a href="{{ path('card_deck') }}" class="btn btn-primary">View Deck</a>
    <a href="{{ path('deck_shuffle') }}" class="btn btn-secondary">Shuffle</a>
    <a href="{{ path('deck_draw') }}" class="btn btn-success">Draw Card</a>
</p>

<hr>

<h2>Class Structure</h2>

<p>The card game is built using four classes organized with inheritance and composition:</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Deck</strong> — The base class representing a single card. Holds a suit and a value (e.g. Hearts / A).</li>
    <li><strong>DeckGraphic</strong> — Extends <code>Deck</code>. Overrides <code>getAsString()</code> to return a Unicode card symbol (e.g. 🂱). Also provides a <code>getColor()</code> method for red/black suits.</li>
    <li><strong>DeckOfCards</strong> — Composed of 52 <code>DeckGraphic</code> objects. Handles the full deck: initialization, shuffling and drawing cards.</li>
    <li><strong>DeckHand</strong> — Composed of <code>DeckGraphic</code> objects. Represents a player's hand of drawn cards.</li>
</ul>

<h2>UML Class Diagram</h2>

<img src="{{ asset('img/uml.png') }}" alt="UML Class Diagram">
</div>


{% endblock %}